DevOps Interview Command Series — Armada (Day 17) 🚢

Armada is a batch workload scheduler for Kubernetes.
It’s used when you need to queue, prioritize, and schedule large-scale jobs efficiently across clusters.

If you’re preparing for DevOps / SRE / Platform interviews, these are the Armada commands & concepts you must know:

armadactl version

armadactl submit job.yaml
armadactl submit job.yaml --queue queue-name

armadactl get queues
armadactl get jobs --queue queue-name
armadactl get job job-id

armadactl cancel job-id
armadactl reprioritize job-id --priority 100

armadactl watch job-id

kubectl get pods -n armada
kubectl get events
kubectl describe pod pod-name


🎯 Interview Focus
• What problem Armada solves vs native Kubernetes Jobs
• Queues, priorities & fairness scheduling
• Handling large-scale batch & ML workloads
• Multi-tenant Kubernetes scheduling
• Debugging pending or failed jobs
• Armada vs Argo Workflows vs CronJobs
